course: dictionary
lesson: 2612
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it and look for clues: who is playing, where it is, what someone is wearing. «Derbies are games between local rivals; rivalry is fine as banter, not as fights or hate.» Here derby means a sports match between two local teams, and rivals are teams that compete against each other.
explain: Use the swap check: put your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense. A capital letter is a clue too. «The biscuit tin in Derby was empty.» There is no match and no hat here, so Derby, with a capital D, must be the name of a city in England.
explain: Some meanings belong to a special world, such as horse racing or old-fashioned clothes. In a story, a man in a derby hat looks old-fashioned, so the hat is the clue. People also say local derby, derby day and roller derby. When the clues are not enough, a dictionary can tell you what the word means.
fact: A word can have several meanings, so always check the context.
fact: A derby is a sports match between two local teams from the same city or area, often very exciting.
fact: The Derby in England is a famous horse race run at Epsom.
fact: A derby is also a hard, round, black hat with a narrow brim; in the UK it is called a bowler hat.
fact: Derby with a capital D is a city in England.
exercise: «Derbies are games between local rivals; rivalry is fine as banter, not as fights or hate.» What is a derby in this sentence? | A city in England | A hard, round, black hat | *A sports match between two local teams | A famous horse race
exercise: «The biscuit tin in Derby was empty.» What is Derby in this sentence? | A horse race | A kind of hat | *A city in England | A sports match between local teams
exercise: In a story, a man wears a derby and looks old-fashioned. What is the derby? | A horse race at Epsom | *A hard, round, black hat with a narrow brim | A racing go-kart | A football team
test: «In the USA, children race homemade go-karts in a soapbox derby.» What does derby mean here? | A city | A horse race at Epsom | *A race or contest open to many people | A hat
test: Which derby is a horse race run at Epsom in England? | A roller derby | *The Derby | A bowler hat | A soapbox derby
exam: Lena reads «The Kentucky Derby is a famous race in the USA.» What does derby mean here? | A city in England | *A famous horse race | A sports match between two local teams | A hard, round, black hat
